# npm packages installed into the mise-managed Node for tool use.
# NOT for project dependencies — use a per-project package.json for those.
#
# mise installs these automatically when provisioning a new Node version
# (node.default_packages_file in config.toml).
# To install into the current Node without re-provisioning:
#   npm install -g --ignore-scripts $(grep -v '^#' ~/.config/mise/default-node-packages | grep -v '^$')
#
# (intentionally empty — mise's aqua/ubi/npm backends cover the tools that need
#  a global npm install; pi is NOT one of them any more (it owns itself via its
#  managed installer — see base/pi/README.md and the pi note in config.toml).
#  Add npm-based tools here only when mise has no backend for them.)
